Subject: [PATCH 23/31] esp: model Sun DATA DMA time with device-owned lifecycle

Instantaneous Sun ESP DMA completion exposes an interrupted lock-holder race
in NEXTSTEP's original SCSA driver. Give Sun4m transfers aggregate 5 MB/s bus
time without modifying the guest or delaying other ESP adapters by default.

Own the timer per controller; gate all DMA entry points, including backend
callbacks. Cancel deferred work on request cancellation/completion, command
replacement and reset. Chip reset also cancels its outstanding SCSI request.
Migrate the virtual deadline in an optional subsection, requiring matching
configuration and rejecting inconsistent restored timer state.

This is aggregate DATA IN/OUT TI timing, not a REQ/ACK or FIFO timing model.
NCR 53C90A/B's guide documents finite asynchronous transfer rates, reset to
disconnected state and DMA count reload. The timer and migration are QEMU
implementation choices. See docs/risc.md in this patchset repo
for hardware references, test evidence and remaining emulation limits.

